  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe `GTELaunchpadV2Pair` contract functions as a liquidity pair for the GTE AMM, similar to Uniswap V2 pairs. It also modifies the Uniswap V2 Pair logic by charging an additional **launchpad fee**. This fee should normally be distributed directly to the launchpad whenever `_update` is called. However, if two or more state-changing calls (e.g., swap, mint+swap, or burn+swap) occur within the same block, then `timeElapsed == 0`. In that case, instead of being distributed, the launchpad fee is only accrued and virtually subtracted from reserves.\n\nThe problem arises because this undistributed fee is reflected in the reserves (can be reserve0 or reserve1) because it is artificially subtracted but not in the balances because the `balanceOf` function provides full balances. \n\n`_update` function's fee accrual logic:-\n```solidity\n if (timeElapsed > 0 && _reserve0 != 0 && _reserve1 != 0) {\n            // * never overflows, and + overflow is desired\n            price0CumulativeLast += uint256(UQ112x112.encode(_reserve1).uqdiv(_reserve0)) * timeElapsed;\n            price1CumulativeLast += uint256(UQ112x112.encode(_reserve0).uqdiv(_reserve1)) * timeElapsed;\n\n            if (launchpadFeeDistributor > address(0)) {\n                if (totalLaunchpadFee0 | totalLaunchpadFee1 > 0) {\n                    delete accruedLaunchpadFee0;\n                    delete accruedLaunchpadFee1;\n                    _distributeLaunchpadFees(totalLaunchpadFee0, totalLaunchpadFee1);\n                }\n            }\n        } else if (launchpadFeeDistributor > address(0) && newLaunchpadFee0 | newLaunchpadFee1 > 0) {\n            accruedLaunchpadFee0 = totalLaunchpadFee0;\n            accruedLaunchpadFee1 = totalLaunchpadFee1;\n            emit LaunchpadFeesAccrued(newLaunchpadFee0, newLaunchpadFee1);\n        }\n\n```\n\nThe undistributed fee completely breaks the fee mechanism, depletes LP shares value and leads to Indirect Fee theft.\nThis happens when there is some accrued fee which is undistributed (because of same block execution of transactions), **if the very next call to the contract happens to be a `swap` function call, then the undistributed fee in the contract is counted as `amountIn` (can be amount0In or amount1In) for this call because of how amountIns are counted**. \n\nHow `amountIns` are calculated in `swap` function\n\n```solidity\n     uint256 amount0In = balance0 > _reserve0 - amount0Out ? balance0 - (_reserve0 - amount0Out) : 0;\n      uint256 amount1In = balance1 > _reserve1 - amount1Out ? balance1 - (_reserve1 - amount1Out) : 0;\n```\nWorse, because the inflated `amountIn` also generates new launchpad fees, the system enters a **fee-on-fee feedback loop**. Over time this depletes LP share value, corrupts pricing, and enables direct financial exploitation\n\nImpact:-\n\n**1. Financial Loss and Dilution**: The pool over-deducts fees (e.g., 1e13 per incident in the PoC,       scaling to 1e15+ for large swaps), transferring extra to the launchpad and diluting LP shares (K increases less than expected, eroding value over time).\n\n**2. Exploitation for Profit**: Attackers can front-run to trigger fee-on-fee and claim inflated outputs/LP tokens (e.g., netting 1e13-1e14 per large tx via precise amountOut). Sync theft allows stealing undistributed fees (e.g., 1e15 from a big accrual) by inflating reserves for LPs.\n\n**3. Broader Risks**: Skews price oracles (TWAP), enables griefing (force over-deduction to manipulate prices), and erodes trust in the AMM. In high-volume pools, cumulative losses could reach significant values; exploitable via MEV for repeated attacks.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nModify `amountIn` calculation to exclude accrued fees e.g.,\n```solidity \namountIn = balance - (reserve + accruedLaunchpadFee)\n```\nCompute new fees only on true deposits, then add to accrued for distribution.\n\nThis looks the best method as of now.",
